#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "376b8af6-29bc-55ae-be7a-9659c2559891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303289} {:answer/id #uuid "38f1d0b5-d56f-5080-be06-dd709d489c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38f1d0b5-d56f-5080-be06-dd709d489c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303290} :answer-field/id #uuid "1965bafe-8660-507f-9547-8ea44caad029" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9258d52-01b3-55d0-afcb-ea66a3cfa2e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-316584" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/assets/f38424364e3d4efd8ebc416974163e3eb87b3350c0c6b8ec7f5ae4ea69339824.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1acae1bf-d135-5b00-abd7-116442570359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363846} {:answer/id #uuid "85c328f9-e1f4-5c86-92b7-3b89061d1e0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85c328f9-e1f4-5c86-92b7-3b89061d1e0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363847} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a80800f-0444-5572-9507-af607ca3a4cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d434700e-c032-526a-98a8-7c986c7c3b34" :question/math-academy-id "q-316597" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/assets/0c8048c789a15d2cfbcdbabce65d256ba1bcda14bc4a02067a2ef9f2287e0656.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\pi {r}^{2}=\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}=9\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 3=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-5\\,|\\cdot 9\\pi  \\\\  & =45\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58a57aef-9201-5a72-8ded-2770500874e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58a57aef-9201-5a72-8ded-2770500874e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363850} :answer-field/id #uuid "e03fea75-0aac-5410-a1f5-360dcc1244cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd127750-f2ea-5566-a4e8-6a3ea17df69e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316599" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-5)\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot 2=30-8=22.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,22\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4feb6eca-9baf-537a-bd96-4e75951c9f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363853} {:answer/id #uuid "861fc691-bc44-5884-aa45-fe3dda66296d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "861fc691-bc44-5884-aa45-fe3dda66296d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363854} :answer-field/id #uuid "61833109-c1bc-500b-ac07-6456a7f484a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e37ea72-4527-59b0-9b76-eb7bab82018e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316602" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-8)\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 3=-40.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-40\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c31dcc-393d-54d7-a1d0-1a9b0f4bf516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11c31dcc-393d-54d7-a1d0-1a9b0f4bf516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348669} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b95e50a-f902-597a-ab12-0718f1ce8489" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cbba01bc-4eb3-5032-90e4-0dfde064bcd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-316609" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,2),(5,2),(4,5).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/assets/aef99dd5276166e5c7b4fb2f716b060390b6577f2d3625dd5dc835bcec6c4856.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-5)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
